====================================================
POINT 4 - SUPERVISED LEARNING - TEACHER GIVES ANSWER
====================================================
Meaning: You give data + answer also, model learns pattern.

Example:
- You give: CIBIL 750 -> Loan Approved = Yes
- You give: CIBIL 550 -> Loan Approved = No
- Model learns: If CIBIL > 650, Approve.

Practice - Your First AI Model - Loan Approval:
Input Code:
import pandas as pd
from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression

# Data - X = CIBIL, y = Approved or Not
X = [[750], [680], [550], [720], [600]]
y = [1, 1, 0, 1, 0]  # 1 = Yes, 0 = No

model = LogisticRegression()
model.fit(X, y)  # Training - Model learns

# Prediction - New person CIBIL 700, will loan approve?
print(model.predict([[700]]))  # Output: [1] = Yes
print(model.predict([[500]]))  # Output: [0] = No

Output:
[1]
[0]

Meaning: CIBIL 700 = Approved Yes, CIBIL 500 = Rejected No.
This is your first AI model. 5 lines only.

